HEAD:docs/history/v1/traceability/ieee1722_1-2021.md:255:| AEM-1 | 7.2.1 | ENTITY descriptor (ids, capabilities, counts, names) consistent with ADP | the processor's DRAM descriptor store (the local `aem_store` ROM + its dynamic overlays were deleted 2026-08-13) | 🟡 SERVABLE, NOT SUPPLIED — `READ_DESCRIPTOR` is implemented again, so the engine will serve this descriptor byte-for-byte out of the DRAM image. What is missing is the image: the descriptor is still GENERATED and still gated in the builder, but nothing in this repository converts that output into the processor's memory image or loads it, so on a stock build the read answers `BAD_ARGUMENTS` (an unloaded image reports a configuration count of zero, and that check precedes the locate). Grade this row against a loaded image, and note that no such image has been built here. **"Consistent with ADP" was BROKEN on silicon 2026-08-14 and is now gated:** the served ENTITY descriptor carried 44 zero bytes across `entity_id` … `association_id` while ADP advertised the real values, because `gen_aem_store` zero-fills those spans for the read-time overlay mux (`KL_aecp_aem_dyn_mux`, deleted 2026-08-13) and the image path never picked the step up. `entity_capabilities` = 0 clears AEM_SUPPORTED, so the entity model was advertising that it has no entity model. `avdecc/gen_aemi_image.py` now bakes every Table 7-2 field into the image from the artifacts ADP is built from. Below: model/builder checks still run, every RTL and SILICON leg is historic (RTL deleted 2026-08-13): ✅ builder gate 28 (identity read back out of the packed image vs `milan-entity.conf` / `adp_shape_defaults.svh` / `pp_adp_pkg.sv` / the config MAC, all 4 configs); ✅ RTL aecp vs `aem_golden.h`; SILICON Hive full enumerate; BENCH | 7.2.1 is the enumeration root; ADP/ENTITY mismatches are the first thing BENCH flags. Table 7-2 states field by field that these "is the same as the … field in ATDECC Discovery Protocol", so a zero here is a direct violation and not merely an omission. |
